// methods become closures on it and the (implicitly static final) constants become
// its properties. It has no constructor, so a class implementing it does not chain
// to one; putting it on the implementor's __super chain is what makes the default
// methods reachable and `instanceof` answer true.
// MEASURED: the InterfaceSkip / EnumSkip fallbacks - LeadMods ... SkipBlock, a
// balanced skip over any body the member set declines - are GONE. They cost the
// three reject files InitializerNotAllowed, EnumConstantExpected and
// EnumConstantNotExpected, because a body javac's parser refuses was swallowed
// whole by the skip; removing them is 3 reject files gained for 1 must-parse
// file lost (DefaultAllowedInIntfAnnotationMember, which the interpreter half
// does not parse either), and it is what makes the two halves agree file for
// file on the corpus.
Interface   = InterfaceReal ;
InterfaceReal <~~ push(makeInterfaceStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = LeadMods KwInterface Id <~~ push(up.in); jEnterClass(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ]
