// descriptor under the constant's name. The constants are built in textual order, so
// __eord (ordinal()) is their index and __values (values()) their list; name() and
// valueOf() read the same two. A constant with its own BODY gets a per-constant
// descriptor whose __super is the enum, so its overrides win over the enum's methods.
EnumDecl    = EnumReal ;
EnumReal    <~~ push(makeEnumStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = LeadMods KwEnum Id <~~ push(up.in); jEnterClass(up.in) ~~> [ ImplementsSkip ]
